WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.208
Multiples are the numbers in a times table.

2
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.686
Count up in 4s.

3
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:18.014
Now count up in 6s.

4
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.136
Look for a number in BOTH lists.

5
00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:28.083
24 is in both lists...

6
00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:34.225
...but 12 comes first. It is the smallest.

7
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.801
So the LCM of 4 and 6 is 12.

8
00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.122
Why do we need it? To add fractions!

9
00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:48.097
The slices are different sizes.

10
00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.460
We can't add them yet.

11
00:00:51.433 --> 00:00:55.473
Cut both pizzas into 12 slices. 12 is the LCM!

12
00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:03.854
1/4 is the same as 3/12. 1/6 is the same as 2/12.

13
00:01:04.833 --> 00:01:07.109
Now the slices match. Just add them.

14
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.933
Find the LCM of the bottoms. Then add!
